  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Legal Aid Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Laos):  The USAID Legal Aid Support activity helps Laos promote the rule of law through a more consistent, fair and transparent delivery of justice in accordance with the law and promote- inclusivity of women, the poor, and traditionally underserved populations. The activity works with the Government of Laos (GOL) to improve the country&apos;s legal aid system by training legal providers at the central and provincial levels, and enhancing legal awareness and access to legal aid services. The activity also assists with budget advocacy for the government&apos;s legal aid fund to ensure that such services are sustained long-term. Legal Aid Support works to reduce the vulnerability to human trafficking among targeted populations in Laos. Training, technical assistance, and professional development of lawyers, judges, and the Ministry of Justice&apos;s legal aid officers (at the provincial and district level) better protects the rights of trafficking in persons (TIP) victims or individuals vulnerable to TIP, particularly women and girls.  Village mediators learn to improve their skills in victim-centers and trauma-informed services. By supporting the GOL&apos;s efforts for Laos to become a &quot;rule of law country&quot;, and by improving citizens&apos; understanding of their rights and obligations under the law, USAID Legal Aid Support contributes to implementation of the Indo-Pacific Strategy. The activity also aligns with the United State Government (USG) Strategy on Women, Peace, and Security by seeking to increase participation of women in preventing, mediating, and resolving conflicts. It is essential to expand the geographical scope and duration of the activity to help Laos move toward a stronger application of the rule of law.. .</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives for Laos: The USAID Legal Aid Support activity aims to: 1) Strengthens the Ministry of Justice, Lao Bar Association and Non-Profit Associations; 2) Increases access to legal aid services; 3) Increases sensitivity to women&#x2019;s rights and empowerment in law-related professions.</narrative>
  </description>
